   {"review":"Section 1 scored nothing this week — the ledger is unavailable and carries zero settled and zero open commitments, so there is no call to settle first, no largest miss to name and no receipt to cite; this is the first weekly filed on B-2026-09-06-weekly and the outcome record begins empty.","outlook":"下周展望. The frame ranks rates first: DGS10 eased against its prior into a quiet tape, and with VIXCLS also lower the read is complacent rather than stressed — I continue that, watching the 9/16 FOMC hike print as the one thing that reprices the long end. The policy.path row carries a hike probability above a coin-flip into 9/16 with no prior to anchor it; I strengthen because a >50% hike sitting under falling vol is an unstable pair, and the observable is whether the front FOMC forecast holds through next week's data. Credit did nothing worth reversing; the HY spread row stays continue, watched via any widening ahead of the meeting. Vol continue: the drop is the tell that nobody is hedging the FOMC yet, observable is whether VIXCLS turns up into 9/16. Dealer.positioning: the gamma flip sat just under spot and drifted, continue, watch whether SPY holds above the flip. On sectors, the week's leadership is unmistakably up-cap-chain: Foundry, Memory/Storage and Computer/GPU all beat SPY hard while Cybersecurity and Software/SaaS were the deep laggards. I strengthen sector:Foundry — INTC, TSM, TSEM, UMC moved as a bloc (4 of 4), and the observable is whether the group holds its lead into the 10-14/10-15 ASML and TSM prints. I strengthen sector:Memory/Storage on the same 4-of-4 breadth, observable being MU's 9/30 read. I fade sector:Cybersecurity — a group down as one (4 of 4) with no dated catalyst to defend it is rotation, not noise; observable is whether NET/CRWD/PANW stop underperforming SPY. I fade sector:Software/SaaS on the same logic, watching whether ADBE's 9/10 print arrests the group's decline. Cloud/Hyperscaler and Semi-Cap/EDA lagged modestly; I fade both softly, observable being ORCL 9/10 and ASML 10-14 respectively. Foundation-Model-Proxy and Devices/Endpoint were roughly benchmark; continue. The el-nino-ag theme printed a large one-week excess in its first full week; I strengthen it, observable being whether NOAA ONI stays above threshold and CBOT grains hold above their 20-day.","catalysts":"Two dated prints land next week, both 2026-09-10 post-close: ADBE and ORCL earnings. Then FOMC 9/16 carries a hike forecast — the single macro event that reprices the rates and policy rows. Further out and admitted: MU earnings 2026-09-30, then ASML 2026-10-14 pre and TSM 2026-10-15, which read through to the Foundry and Semi-Cap/EDA rows. The 9/10 pair and the 9/16 meeting are the whole near story; everything else is October.","coverage":[{"id":"rates.front","token":"untested","p":0.60,"why":"DGS2 not ingested; no datum handed","observable":"front-end yield once DGS2 series returns"},{"id":"rates.long","token":"continue","p":0.62,"why":"long yield eased into quiet tape, no stress","observable":"DGS10 direction into FOMC 9/16"},{"id":"curve.shape","token":"untested","p":0.60,"why":"2s10s uncomputable without DGS2","observable":"curve once front-end series is ingested"},{"id":"policy.path","token":"strengthen","p":0.58,"why":"above-even hike under falling vol is unstable pair","observable":"whether hike forecast holds into 9/16"},{"id":"credit","token":"continue","p":0.66,"why":"HY spread barely moved, no widening","observable":"spread widening ahead of FOMC"},{"id":"vol","token":"continue","p":0.64,"why":"vol drop signals nobody hedging the meeting","observable":"VIXCLS turning up into 9/16"},{"id":"dealer.positioning","token":"continue","p":0.60,"why":"gamma flip drifted just under spot","observable":"SPY holding above the flip level"},{"id":"flow","token":"untested","p":0.55,"why":"net premium has no prior observation to compare","observable":"tide sign versus a future reading"},{"id":"commodities","token":"untested",